<title>SWITZERLAND: Clariant approves Hoechst deal.</title>
<headline>Clariant approves Hoechst deal.</headline>
<dateline>MUTTENZ, Switzerland 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss chemicals group Clariant AG said on Wednesday its board approved the incorporation of Hoechst AG's specialty chemicals business into Clariant.</p>
<p>The Clariant board had already agreed in principle to the deal. Last December Hoechst agreed to sell its specialty chemicals group to Clariant and to retain a minority stake in the Swiss group.</p>
<p>Clariant said in a statement today that the proposal would be submitted to its shareholders for approval at the annual general meeting scheduled for April 29.</p>
<p>The Hoechst supervisory board approved the transaction on March 11 and it intends to submit it to shareholders at its annual general meeting, scheduled for May 6.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
